From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:04:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] l2mcd: drop the parts of #24327 that are not snooping

The PR branch carries four changes from other work on the same fork.
None is needed for IGMP/MLD snooping and each changes the image's
behaviour, so they are taken out:

- rules/config: ENABLE_TRANSLIB_WRITE = y (gNMI translib write access)
  goes back to commented out, the 202511 default.
- dockers/docker-sonic-gnmi/telemetry_vars.j2: the "is defined" guards
  belong to the closed gNMI PR (#24328); back to 202511.
- src/sonic-yang-models/yang-models/sonic-device_metadata.yang: the
  x509 container is gNMI certificate config, same origin; back to
  202511.
- files/build_templates/init_cfg.json.j2: a default MGMT_PORT|eth0 with
  admin_status up. A switch that keeps its management port down on
  purpose would have it brought up by the image's defaults; removed.
  The l2mcd FEATURE entry (state disabled) in the same file stays.

After this the series diff against 202511 is the l2mcd container, its
rules, service, CoPP trap group, rsyslog/logrotate lines and the two
snooping YANG models with their sample config.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
